==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Superstar Koneko''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Using Koneko revolves around understanding your odds. She is essentially a pseudo–slot machine of damage abilities—each triggering independently and creating an overwhelming kaleidoscope of possibilities, from everything activating at once to nothing at all. The only thing that changes between her forms is stats, standing range, cost and recharge.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Koneko is more spammable, with a relatively short standing range of 250 in comparison to Superstar Koneko's 450. She has an expected DPS of ~6.6k against her target enemy (the one that is hit by her [[Single Attack]]) and ~3.1k DPS to surrounding enemies at Lv.30, with the same abilities as her Evolved Form. Her shorter recharge time makes her generally better for Metal enemies than her Evolved Form, considering the fact that every common Metal is outranged by this form. [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] can also give her the opportunity to snipe [[Koronium]] (and by extention most of the [[Kory]] variants) from a distance.

It is important to note that her matchups against her target traits are generally far worse than Superstar Koneko's due to a lack of range and damage. Outside of Metals, this makes her only good for peon control against rushers like [[Bore Jr.]] and [[Sir Rel]], or to infiltrate enemy blind spots, as almost every other relevant Traitless and Relic threat outranges her. While she is more spammable, she still has a cooldown of 1 minute. It's not recommended to use this form over the Evolved one, as she fares much worse in every regard despite being far cheaper.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Although Superstar Koneko's many abilities complicate things, you can expect an average DPS of ~14.5k to her target enemy, and ~6.8k DPS to surrounding enemies at Lv.30. Given her abilities and probabilities, it's impossible to predict exactly what will happen on each attack; her damage can go from a measly 11.6k per hit to about '''30 times''' that amount at ~349.4k damage if everything connects!
<!--Calculation of expected DPS at lv.30 with intermediate values rounded to 2 decimal places

Raw Dmg = 11645

Find multipliers for the Critical and Savage Blow multipliers respectively:

Expected = 2 * Raw * Chance + Raw * (1 - Chance) = Raw * (2 * Chance + 1 - Chance) = Raw * (Chance + 1)
Expected / Raw = Chance + 1

Expected = 3 * Raw * Chance + Raw * (1 - Chance) = Raw * (3 * Chance + 1 - Chance) = Raw * (2 * Chance + 1)
Expected / Raw = 2 * Chance + 1

Include Critical (12%, x2, multiplier 1.12) and Savage Blow (22%, x3, multiplier 1.44). This is done before Wave, Surge, Explosion as they are carried on.

Intermediate Dmg = Raw Dmg * (1.12) * (1.44) = 18781.06

Calculate additional expected damage from Wave (22%), Surge (22%, level 2), Explosion (22%). Koneko's Surge has a 100% chance of hitting which simplifies this a little.

Wave Dmg = Intermediate Dmg * 0.22 = 4131.83
Surge Dmg = Intermediate Dmg * 0.22 * 2 = 8263.66
Explosion Dmg = Intermediate Dmg * 0.22 = 4131.83

These values are summed to get the expected attack.

Expected Dmg = Intermediate Dmg + Wave Dmg + Surge Dmg + Explosion Dmg = 35308.38

Finally, the expected DPS is this divided by attack frequency (then multiplied by 30 if frame count is used).

Expected DPS = 35308.38 / 73 * 30 = 14510.29-->

Her [[Slow]] effect against target traits can be considered a bonus, since none of her other abilities are trait-dependent. Even so, as a backliner this makes her excellent at countering midrangers like [[H. Nah]], [[Mr. Mer]], and [[M. Ost]]/[[R.Ost]], with the Slow uptime approaching 100% depending on her procs. That said, bad luck might sometimes be fatal if no useful abilities proc when you need them.

More often than not you will be using her for general DPS rather than CC, but in both scenarios, her strength (and her detriment) lies in how many of her abilities decide to land. She can be as good or bad as your luck is at that specific moment, which ultimately leaves it up to the player to determine whether her utilities are too inconsistent to be used practically. It can be very easy to overestimate/underestimate what can and can't happen with her. Treat her as a clutch tool, and try to keep her alive as long as possible with other support options like the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to maximize the amount of attacks she can do.

Be mindful of her recharge time: if she dies, she is not coming back for a very long time.

==='''Ability Chances'''===
<!-- We're not having edit wars. Round everything to 2 s.f.
Formulae are in Python.

from math import comb, log10, floor
import re
def sf(n: float):
    dp = abs(floor(log10(n)) + 1)
    search = str(round(float(n) * 100, dp))
    pattern = r"[0\.]*[1-9]\.*\d"
    return re.match(pattern, search).group(0) + "%"
-->''General Ability Activation'': On average, you can expect her to activate at least one ability about '''~67%''' of the time. Since each ability increases DPS in some way, the more that trigger, the merrier.
<!-- 1 - ((1 - 0.22)**4 * (1 - 0.12)) -->

''AoE Abilities'': The chance to activate at least one AoE ability ([[Wave Attack|Wave]], [[Surge Attack|Surge]], or [[Explosion]]) is '''~53%''' overall.
<!-- 1 - (1 - 0.22)**3 -->

*One AoE ability: '''~40%''' <!-- 0.22 * (1 - 0.22)**2 * comb(3, 1) -->
*Two AoE abilities: '''~11%''' <!-- 0.22**2 * (1 - 0.22) * comb(3, 2) -->
*All three AoE abilities: '''~1.1%''' <!-- 0.22**3 -->

Each individual AoE ability has its own merits and disadvantages in specific situations, so you should know exactly what to look for all at times. Explosions can double dip on enemies knocked back by the initial blast's hit, Wave Attacks don't have a finicky range quirk which means they can consistently hit enemies directly in front of her, and Surge Attacks have the highest DPS by proxy of hitting twice for full damage and creating an area of denial.

''Savage Blows and Critical Hits Solo VS AoE'': On their own, [[Savage Blow|Savage Blows]] and [[Critical Hit]]s are largely inefficient. They typically waste an attack if not bundled with an AoE effect (which compensates for her Single Attack nature). With this, it is worth noting that any given attack has a '''~31%''' chance of containing either a Savage Blow, Critical Hit, or both. In most situations, Savage Blows tend to be more advantageous thanks to their higher damage multiplier.
<!-- 1 - (1 - 0.22) * (1 - 0.12) -->

''Critical Hit with AoE'': A Critical Hit occurring alongside an AoE ability is '''~6.3%''' (without Critical Hit chance [[Cat Combo]]s). Don't rely on this happening to clear out hordes of Metal enemies. But if it does, the damage is potent enough to nearly wipe out all Metal enemies on the field.
<!-- (1 - (1 - 0.22)**3) * 0.12 -->

''Savage Blows plus Critical Hits'': Managing to score a Savage Blow and Critical Hit in the same attack leads to a final damage multiplier of 6x Koneko's base attack. On average, this only happens '''~2.6%''' of the time, making it incredibly rare; as discussed previously, this effect can go to waste if there's no AoE to accompany it. Thus, the odds that it also includes any AoE attack make this number drop to a measly '''~1.4%''' chance.
<!--
Base: (1 - (1 - 0.22)) * (1 - (1 - 0.12))
With AoE: (1 - (1 - 0.22)**3) * 0.22 * 0.12
-->

''All Effects Proc Simultaneously'': The odds that every effect procs at once is only '''0.028%''', or roughly a '''1 in 3,557''' chance per attack. Don't expect this to ever happen: it will take an average of 2 hours and 24 minutes if she's constantly attacking.
<!-- 0.22 * 0.12 * 0.22 * 0.22 * 0.22 -->

