==Trivia==
*The ''neko'' in Moneko's, Neneko's and Koneko's names means "cat", likely referencing the fact that they are ''[[wikipedia:Catgirl|Nekomimi]]'', or people with the ears and tail of a cat.
**The first two letters in each of their names spell out "Moneko" when put together.
**According to たまさん, one of The Battle Cats' main artists, Koneko's design was already created by the time Neneko was implemented, but took several years to be added for an unknown reason.<ref>[https://x.com/tamasanp/status/1893341129166246173?s=20]</ref>
*"Gives it all for her fans" may hint at Superstar Koneko's Savage Blow ability, whose Japanese name (渾身の一撃 ''Konshin no Ichigeki'') translates to "All-Out Blow". 渾身 ''Konshin'' means "(putting in) all one's efforts" or "(using) all one's might".
*Given [[Teacher Bun Bun]]'s gargoyle-like appearance, the Bun Bun guarding Superstar Koneko may be a reference to how gargoyles were believed to protect against evil.
*She is the only character who has all three "post-attack area damage" abilities ([[Wave Attack]], [[Surge Attack]] and [[Explosion]]). The same for [[Critical Hit]] and [[Savage Blow]].
*Koneko is tied with [[Metal Maiden Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Metal Maiden Koneko]] for the cheapest cost of any obtainable [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]], at only 148¢.
*Koneko is the only non-collab Uber Rare Cat to be featured in [[Daily Bonus|Login Stamp]] backgrounds and a stage background, appearing in all of the levels in [[Koneko Music Festival#Koneko Takes the Stage|Koneko Takes the Stage]].

